    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d975">

                <pb facs="0945" n="847" xml:id="pg847"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Duarte.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 87.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 21st instant, informing me of the deposit of the money
                    awarded by the Delagoa Bay arbitration.</p>
                <p>As heretofore stated, the Government of the United States is not to be understood
                    as authorizing or acquiescing in the making of said deposit, and in
                    acknowledging the same it does so without prejudice and with reservation of all
                    its rights, of whatever nature or character they may be, in the premises.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
